                '    <figcaption class="text-xs text-gray-500 text-center mt-2 px-2">End-to-end WHMCS automation '
                'pipeline from client order to autonomous lifecycle renewal.</figcaption>\n'
                '  </figure>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Connecting WHMCS to cPanel &amp; WHM via '
                'Secure API Tokens</h2>\n'
                '  <p>To enable instant account provisioning without storing root passwords in your database, connect '
                'WHMCS using cPanel API Tokens:</p>\n'
                '  <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6">\n'
                '    <li>Log into your WHM root interface and navigate to <strong>Development &gt; Manage API '
                'Tokens</strong>.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Generate a new token with permissions restricted to account creation, suspension, and '
                'password modification.</li>\n'
                '    <li>In your WHMCS admin panel, navigate to <strong>Setup &gt; Products/Services &gt; '
                'Servers</strong> and click "Add New Server".</li>\n'
                '    <li>Select "cPanel" from the module dropdown, enter your server hostname and IP, and paste the '
                'API Token into the Access Hash/Token field.</li>\n'
                '    <li>Test the connection to ensure that WHMCS can query package plans directly from your '
                'server.</li>\n'
                '  </ol>\n'
                '  <p>When clients purchase hosting packages, WHMCS executes the API call in under 5 seconds, emailing '
                'the customer their cPanel login credentials and server nameservers immediately.</p>\n'
                '</section>\n'
                '\n'
                '<section class="space-y-4">\n'
                '  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Automating Software License Provisioning for '
                'VPS Hosting</h2>\n'
                '  <p>If you offer virtual private servers or dedicated cloud instances, customers frequently require '
